<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>VBench Results</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further evaluate these approaches on VBench-1.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> and VBench-2.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> suites with their standard prompts and official scorers. Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.3 VBench Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SARA: Semantically Adaptive Relational Alignment for Video Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports the VBench-1.0 <em id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Semantic</em> aggregate, the VBench-2.0 dimension scores, and the VBench-2.0 <em id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Final</em> score, with per-task breakdowns in App. <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 VBench-1.0 per-task semantic scores ‣ Appendix D More results ‣ SARA: Semantically Adaptive Relational Alignment for Video Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and App. <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 VBench-2.0 per-task scores ‣ Appendix D More results ‣ SARA: Semantically Adaptive Relational Alignment for Video Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Both VBench protocols agree with the VLM rubric: SARA has the best aggregate score on each, leading VBench-1.0 <em id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Semantic</em> by <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.90</annotation></semantics></math> over VideoREPA and VBench-2.0 <em id="S4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Final</em> by <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.38" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.38</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.38</annotation></semantics></math> over MoAlign. Per-dimension scores are more diffuse, as expected for sub-tasks that span very different aspects of generation. The small <em id="S4.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Human Fidelity</em> drop shared by all continually-trained methods is structural to the matched protocol: each approach updates <em id="S4.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only</em> the Wan2.2 high-noise expert while leaving the low-noise expert frozen. Since, anatomical detail is rendered at the low-noise stage of Wan2.2’s two-expert mixture-of-experts (MoE), any high-noise update shifts the intermediate-latent distribution the un-updated low-noise expert was trained against (App. <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Limitations and broader impact ‣ SARA: Semantically Adaptive Relational Alignment for Video Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>). SARA still posts the smallest such drop, consistent with the hypothesis that its text-conditioned routing delivers a more targeted high-noise update. Across all three protocols, SARA is the only method that wins every aggregate score.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Public VBench-1.0 / 2.0 results<span id="S4.T2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (<math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>, higher is better). Best per column in </span>bold<span id="S4.T2.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.</span></span></figcaption>
